title: TKSP/DHKD is founded
new-page: true
on-display: {! if(typeof AnatolianKurdishEventMedia!=="undefined")AnatolianKurdishEventMedia.sync(); !}

= TKSP/DHKD is founded

{!<img src="img/kurdish/dhkd.png" alt="TKSP/DHKD is founded" style="display:block;max-width:100%;max-height:300px;width:auto;height:auto;margin:12px auto;object-fit:contain">!}

A new movement has risen in the unusually active Kurdish political scene. Different factions, associations and organisations aligned with the democratic socialist ''Özgürlük Yolu'' (Path of Freedom) movement have established the underground Türkiye Kürdistanı Sosyalist Partisi (Socialist Party of Turkish Kurdistan, TKSP for short) and it's legal, open-door front organisation, Devrimci Halk Kültür Derneği (Revolutionary People's Cultural Association, DHKD for short). The movement, though illegal, has so far remained peaceful in their methods, preferring nonviolent mass mobilisation and cultural rejuvenation events to armed guerilla warfare.

Descending not from T-KDP but networks of Kurdish activists who left TİP due to their grievances with the party not adopting a clear platform for Kurdish emancipation, TKSP was established under the leadership of Kemal Burkay and follows an uncompromisingly left-wing program. Though the party itself mostly operates as an underground circle of organisers, DHKD has already opened branches in most of our Kurdish-majority regions and have pulled thousands of urban intellectuals, teachers, academicians, youth and artisans into their ranks via their cultural events and mass mobilisation.

